From 67741d45f05971c16c30235bd8736dcdedd799fa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: anyingiit <49945850+anyingiit@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 18:41:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] docs(lib): document the Logos derive macro in rustdoc

The docs of the `Logos` derive macro only listed the helper attributes,
so everything about how to use them lived in the external handbook and
was not available with `cargo doc --offline`.

Add a reference to the re-exported derive macro covering `#[token]` and
`#[regex]` (arguments, `ignore(case)`), token disambiguation and
priorities, callbacks and their return types, and every `#[logos(...)]`
option (skip, extras, error, utf8, lifetime, subpattern, type, crate,
export_dir), with doctested examples taken from or modelled on the
handbook. The crate-level docs now point to it.

Closes #562
---
